# WS3-05 detector expectation (seeded violation). Source: the MC68000 User's Manual
# (a word or long-word access at an odd address raises an address error, exception
# vector 3; the 68020 handles misaligned operands). Expected: under the 68000 the
# program does not print "odd read ..." (an exception or a vamos error); under
# -C 68020 it prints "odd read 515" (0x0203 big-endian). If the 68000 run prints the
# line, vamos cannot detect odd-address accesses and the WS3-05 runtime check is a
# limit (03-01 §Falsifiability); the item then rests on code reading.
expect: script
